## Why This Is Asked
Tests basic Android data persistence and UI wiring using familiar components.

## Key Concepts
- Room: Entity, DAO, database
- LiveData and ViewModel
- Repository pattern
- Prepopulation via RoomDatabase.Callback
- Rotation handling with LiveData

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity
data class Task(
  @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Long = 0,
  val text: String,
  val done: Boolean = false
)
@Dao
interface TaskDao {
  @Query("SELECT * FROM Task") fun getAll(): LiveData<List<Task>>
  @Insert fun insert(task: Task): Long
  @Delete fun delete(task: Task)
}
@Database(entities = [Task::class], version = 1)
abstract class AppDb : RoomDatabase() {
  abstract fun taskDao(): TaskDao
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test prepopulation and DAO methods?
- How would you migration plan for Task schema changes?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design an offline-first data flow, encryption, and conflict handling for a real Android app.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first data modeling and synchronization
- Per-device encryption with Android Keystore
- WorkManager-based background sync
- Per-field conflict resolution (last-write-wins)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: last-write-wins merge for edits
function mergeEdits(local, remote) {
  const out = { ...remote };
  for (const key of Object.keys(local)) {
    const l = local[key];
    const r = remote[key];
    out[key] = (l?.ts > r?.ts) ? l.value : r.value;
  }
  return out;
}
```

